  "verbalization": "Gerontoisoflavone A is shown to have a target relationship with the Insulin receptor-related protein through two distinct pathways. In the first pathway, Gerontoisoflavone A directly targets Mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase 6, which in turn is targeted by a complex compound with a specific chemical structure. This compound then targets the Insulin receptor-related protein. In the second pathway, Gerontoisoflavone A targets ATP-citrate synthase, which is also targeted by the same complex compound, and this compound subsequently targets the Insulin receptor-related protein. Both pathways converge on the Insulin receptor-related protein through the same target compound, suggesting a potential mechanism involving the activation of a signaling cascade through the complex compound. The evidence suggests that Gerontoisoflavone A may influence the Insulin receptor-related protein via a shared pathway involving the complex compound, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
